    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5437A\n\nSPONSOR: CLEARE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the social services law, in relation to allowing\nprospective and current agency personnel complete training through\nremote training methods\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to allow agency personnel to complete neces-\nsary training requirements through remote training methods.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends section 409-g of the social services law to\noutline professions and agency personnel, including caseworkers involved\nin the provision or supervision of preventive services, foster care\nservices and adoption services, to obtain required trainings through\ndistance learning methods.\n\nSection 2 of the bill establishes the effect date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nVoluntary agency staff, similar to county CPS workers are required to\nreceive training related to the safety, permanency and well-being, the\nthree pillars of child welfare practice. Last year, legislation was\nenacted (Chapter 470 of the Laws of 2024) to allow county CPS workers to\ncomplete certain required training through distance learning methods.\nThis same flexibility should apply across the child welfare sector.\n\nAllowing virtual training would remove the geographic and financial\nbarrier that prevents many potential workers from joining these\nprofessions. This bill would increase accessibility, creating the poten-\ntial for more case workers to join in this work. It will help provide\nsome relief to already overburdened work force.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill. Amended 2026 to parallel Chapter 470 of 2024- which modernized\nCPS training requirements\n\n \nFISCAL:\n\nTo Be Determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law. Effective immediately, the addition, amendment and/or\nrepeal of any rule or regulation necessary for the implementation of\nthis act on its effective date are authorized to be made and completed\non or before such date.\n",
